+7 Cleaver is in fact nothing to scoff at, but it's two-handed.
The Sceptre of Might merits consideration, because of its double damage
against non-coaligned monsters, but against lawful enemies it only
does as much damage as a normal mace; Grayswandir's damage is its base,
and gets an extra 10.5 against silver-haters. I might be (I think I am
doing it right though) confusing where the double-damage modifier gets
applied --- if it also applies to your strength bonus, then GS/SoM are
even more clearly superior.

And yes, the Sceptre confers MR when carried.

